// General notes
/*
Dew Point Calculation from http://iridl.ldeo.columbia.edu/dochelp/QA/Basic/dewpoint.html
If you are interested in a simpler calculation that gives an approximation of dew point temperature 
if you know the observed temperature and relative humidity, the following formula was proposed 
in a 2005 article by Mark G. Lawrence in the Bulletin of the American Meteorological Society:

Td = T - ((100 - RH)/5.)
where Td is dew point temperature (in degrees Celsius), 
T is observed temperature (in degrees Celsius), and 
RH is relative humidity (in percent). 


Apparently this relationship is fairly accurate for relative humidity values above 50%.

*/
